# Copy this file to .env.local and paste the real values in.
#
# .env.local is gitignored and never committed. Neither value is ever printed
# by this service, echoed in a response, or written to a log (§10: "The key is
# never typed into a chat. .env.local, Vercel env vars, and a password
# manager.").

# From console.anthropic.com, on the account separate from the Max
# subscription, with a monthly spend limit set. This is the only place the key
# lives besides Vercel and the password manager.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# One secret per calling app. Each app sends its own as
# `Authorization: Bearer <secret>`, from ITS OWN environment variable called
# CAPTURE_TOKEN. The service knows each by the name after the underscore, so
# revoking one app is deleting one line from the service's environment.
# Generate one with:  npm run make-token -- fnd
# With none set, the service accepts nothing and returns 401 (§2.1).
CAPTURE_TOKEN_FND=
CAPTURE_TOKEN_ADHD=

# Optional, and off unless set to 1. Writes one line per request naming the
# calling app — never the token, never the words. For evidencing a migration
# only; outside one, this service writes nothing about who called it or when.
# CAPTURE_LOG_CALLERS=1

# Optional. Defaults to the smallest model; see src/model.ts.
# CAPTURE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
